# Task: explore the business

{% if area %}
The owner wants to explore **{{ area }}** in detail.
{% else %}
The owner wants to explore the whole business, one area at a time.
{% endif %}

## Steps

{% if selected %}
1. Read the area. These queries return every record with its own fields:

{% for e in selected if e.list_query %}
```graphql
query Explore{{ e.name }} {
  {{ e.list_query }} { {{ e.selection() }} }
}
```

{% endfor %}
2. Present each kind as a table. Follow references on request (e.g. a service's
   `category`, `faqs` and `actions`); the `business_schema` prompt lists every field.
3. Offer to drill into a single record (`<entity>(id: ...)`) or to move on to a related
   area.
{% else %}
{% if area %}
There is no area called "{{ area }}". Show the areas below and ask which one to explore.
{% endif %}
1. Show the areas as a table and ask where to start:

| Area | What it covers | Query |
| --- | --- | --- |
{% for title, members in sections %}
| {{ title }} | {{ members | map(attribute="name") | join(", ") }} | {{ members | selectattr("list_query") | map(attribute="list_query") | map("tick") | join(", ") }} |
{% endfor %}

2. For the chosen area, read its records with `{{ tools.query }}`, e.g.:

```graphql
query ExploreServices {
  serviceCategories { id name services { id name summary hidden } }
}
```

3. Present each kind as a table, then offer the next area in the order above.
{% endif %}

